        "status": "source-custody",
        "title": "Human Biology - Overview",
        "updated": "null"
      },
      "text": "Every body system implements **negative feedback control**. The engineering analogy is exact."
    },
    {
      "id": "00-OVERVIEW.md#012",
      "path": [
        "00-OVERVIEW.md"
      ],
      "level": 0,
      "line": 1,
      "metadata": {
        "backsource_ids": "[proof-backfill:human-biology:00-overview, git-history:human-biology:00-overview]",
        "canonical_path": "human-biology/00-OVERVIEW.md",
        "concepts": "[overview]",
        "current_path": "human-biology/00-OVERVIEW.md",
        "id": "maxim:human-biology:overview",
        "index_roles": "[guide, root-concept]",
        "kind": "guide",
        "maxim_schema": "maxim.frontmatter.v1",
        "module": "human-biology",
        "remap_from": "[]",
        "remap_to": "[]",
        "root_concepts": "[overview]",
        "section": "human-biology",
        "source_custody": "partial",
        "status": "source-custody",
        "title": "Human Biology - Overview",
        "updated": "null"
      },
      "text": "```\nSET POINT (reference)\n  -> ERROR DETECTOR\n     compares sensed value with set point\n  -> EFFECTOR\n     actuator: muscle, gland, or organ\n  -> CONTROLLED VARIABLE\n     body state being regulated\n  -> SENSOR (afferent)\n     reports current value back to the detector\n```"
    },
    {
      "id": "00-OVERVIEW.md#013",
      "path": [
        "00-OVERVIEW.md"
      ],
      "level": 0,
      "line": 1,
      "metadata": {
        "backsource_ids": "[proof-backfill:human-biology:00-overview, git-history:human-biology:00-overview]",
        "canonical_path": "human-biology/00-OVERVIEW.md",
        "concepts": "[overview]",
        "current_path": "human-biology/00-OVERVIEW.md",
        "id": "maxim:human-biology:overview",
        "index_roles": "[guide, root-concept]",
        "kind": "guide",
        "maxim_schema": "maxim.frontmatter.v1",
        "module": "human-biology",
        "remap_from": "[]",
        "remap_to": "[]",
        "root_concepts": "[overview]",
        "section": "human-biology",
        "source_custody": "partial",
        "status": "source-custody",
        "title": "Human Biology - Overview",
        "updated": "null"
      },
      "text": "| Controlled variable | Sensor | Set point | Effectors |\n|--------------------|--------|-----------|-----------|\n| Core temperature | Hypothalamic thermoreceptors | ~37°C | Sweat glands, shivering, vasodilation/constriction |\n| Blood glucose | Pancreatic β/α cells | ~90 mg/dL (5 mM) | Insulin (↓ glucose), glucagon (↑ glucose) |\n| Blood pressure | Baroreceptors (aortic arch, carotid sinus) | ~120/80 mmHg | Heart rate, vascular resistance, renal fluid retention |\n| Arterial pCO₂ | Central/peripheral chemoreceptors | ~40 mmHg | Respiratory rate and tidal volume |\n| Blood pH | Renal tubules + chemoreceptors | 7.35–7.45 | H⁺ excretion, HCO₃⁻ reabsorption, ventilation rate |\n| Serum Ca²⁺ | Parathyroid chief cells | 8.5–10.2 mg/dL | PTH → bone resorption, renal Ca²⁺ retention, vit D activation |\n| Blood osmolality | Hypothalamic osmoreceptors | ~285–295 mOsm/kg | ADH (vasopressin) → renal water retention |"
    },
    {
      "id": "00-OVERVIEW.md#014",
      "path": [
        "00-OVERVIEW.md"
      ],
      "level": 0,
      "line": 1,
      "metadata": {
        "backsource_ids": "[proof-backfill:human-biology:00-overview, git-history:human-biology:00-overview]",
