      "text": "## The 4 Tissue Types"
    },
    {
      "id": "00-OVERVIEW.md#017",
      "path": [
        "00-OVERVIEW.md"
      ],
      "level": 0,
      "line": 1,
      "metadata": {
        "backsource_ids": "[proof-backfill:human-biology:00-overview, git-history:human-biology:00-overview]",
        "canonical_path": "human-biology/00-OVERVIEW.md",
        "concepts": "[overview]",
        "current_path": "human-biology/00-OVERVIEW.md",
        "id": "maxim:human-biology:overview",
        "index_roles": "[guide, root-concept]",
        "kind": "guide",
        "maxim_schema": "maxim.frontmatter.v1",
        "module": "human-biology",
        "remap_from": "[]",
        "remap_to": "[]",
        "root_concepts": "[overview]",
        "section": "human-biology",
        "source_custody": "partial",
        "status": "source-custody",
        "title": "Human Biology - Overview",
        "updated": "null"
      },
      "text": "```\n+-------------------+--------------------------------------------------+\n| EPITHELIAL        | Linings, barriers, secretory surfaces            |\n|                   | Skin surface, GI lining, kidney tubules, alveoli |\n|                   | Avascular — no direct blood supply               |\n|                   | Polarity: apical face ≠ basolateral face         |\n|                   | Subtypes: simple/stratified × squamous/cuboidal/ |\n|                   |           columnar                               |\n+-------------------+--------------------------------------------------+\n| CONNECTIVE        | Structure, support, transport, storage           |\n|                   | Bone, cartilage, tendons, adipose, blood, fascia |\n|                   | Defined by extracellular matrix (ECM):           |\n|                   | collagen, elastin, proteoglycans, hydroxyapatite |\n|                   | in bone                                          |\n+-------------------+--------------------------------------------------+\n| MUSCLE            | Contractile force generation                     |\n|                   | Skeletal — voluntary, striated, multinucleated   |\n|                   | Cardiac — involuntary, striated, intercalated    |\n|                   |           discs, one or two nuclei               |\n|                   | Smooth — involuntary, non-striated, single       |\n|                   |          nucleus, organs and vessels             |\n+-------------------+--------------------------------------------------+\n| NERVOUS           | Electrical + chemical signaling                  |\n|                   | Neurons (signal) + glia (support, insulate,      |\n|                   | maintain: astrocytes, oligodendrocytes,          |\n|                   | Schwann cells, microglia)                        |\n|                   | Axon = wire; myelin = insulation; synapse = gap  |\n+-------------------+--------------------------------------------------+\n```"
    },
