        "source_custody": "partial",
        "status": "source-custody",
        "title": "Human Biology - Overview",
        "updated": "null"
      },
      "text": "The body is a fault-tolerant, self-organizing distributed system with ~37 trillion nodes. Every organ system maps cleanly to engineering concepts."
    },
    {
      "id": "00-OVERVIEW.md#028",
      "path": [
        "00-OVERVIEW.md"
      ],
      "level": 0,
      "line": 1,
      "metadata": {
        "backsource_ids": "[proof-backfill:human-biology:00-overview, git-history:human-biology:00-overview]",
        "canonical_path": "human-biology/00-OVERVIEW.md",
        "concepts": "[overview]",
        "current_path": "human-biology/00-OVERVIEW.md",
        "id": "maxim:human-biology:overview",
        "index_roles": "[guide, root-concept]",
        "kind": "guide",
        "maxim_schema": "maxim.frontmatter.v1",
        "module": "human-biology",
        "remap_from": "[]",
        "remap_to": "[]",
        "root_concepts": "[overview]",
        "section": "human-biology",
        "source_custody": "partial",
        "status": "source-custody",
        "title": "Human Biology - Overview",
        "updated": "null"
      },
      "text": "| Body System | Engineering Analog | Key Parallel |\n|-------------|-------------------|--------------|\n| Nervous system | Interrupt-driven event bus | Fast, wired, low-latency; reflexes = hardware interrupts bypassing OS; CNS = event loop |\n| Endocrine system | Pub/sub message queue | Slow broadcast via shared medium (bloodstream); subscribers (receptors) filter by topic |\n| Cardiovascular | Dual-loop hydraulic circuit with centrifugal pump | Two series loops; Poiseuille r⁴ scaling = pipe bandwidth; arterioles = flow control valves |\n| Respiratory | pH buffer + gas exchange membrane | Henderson-Hasselbalch as ratio controller; CO₂ = proxy signal for pH regulation |\n| Immune (innate) | Stateless firewall + IDS | Pattern-matching against PAMPs; no memory between sessions; fast but coarse |\n| Immune (adaptive) | ML classifier with online training | Trains on antigens → clonal expansion → memory; secondary response = cached model |\n| Renal | Filter pipeline with active reclamation | 180 L/day filtered, 99.2% reclaimed; GFR autoregulation = two-feedback pressure regulator |\n| Digestive (liver) | Central data hub | Routing (lipoproteins), transformation (detox), storage (glycogen), logging (bilirubin) |\n| RAAS | Cascading PID controller | Renin → Ang I → Ang II → aldosterone: each step amplifies; negative feedback via BP |\n| Bone remodeling | Adaptive resource allocation | Wolff's law: load-bearing remodels structure (Hebbian for bone); osteocytes = sensors |\n| Homeostasis loops | PID control with set point | Sensor → comparator → effector → controlled variable → feedback (see diagram below) |"
    }
